From: PortareOS <hello@portare.org>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dp: no PUSH_IDLE after an unplug

Pulling a USB-C DisplayPort adapter tells the driver first (the HPD
unplug handler clears plugged), and the CRTC is switched off after
that. .atomic_disable() still pushed the idle pattern, because
power_on stays set until .atomic_post_disable(). By then the sink is
gone and the combo PHY has been switched away from DP: PUSH_IDLE timed
out, and the controller went on raising IDLE_PATTERN_SENT, measured at
72000 interrupts a second on CPU 0, with the controller held runtime
active, until the next plug reset it.

The HPD state machine 7.3 dropped used to skip the push in this case
(hpd_state == ST_DISCONNECT_PENDING). Skip it when the sink is
unplugged.
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
@@ -1482,6 +1482,16 @@
 	if (!dp->power_on)
 		return;
 
+	/*
+	 * Nor after an unplug: the sink is gone and, on USB-C, the PHY has
+	 * already been switched away from DP. PUSH_IDLE then times out, and
+	 * the controller goes on raising IDLE_PATTERN_SENT afterwards, some
+	 * 70000 interrupts a second until the next plug resets it.
+	 */
+	scoped_guard(mutex, &msm_dp_display->plugged_lock)
+		if (!msm_dp_display->plugged)
+			return;
+
 	msm_dp_ctrl_push_idle(msm_dp_display->ctrl);
 }
 
